# SEO-Forge Standards for Cursor

When editing or creating web pages, layout templates, or data models:

1. **Titles & Descriptions**:
   - Every public route must have a `<PageTitle>` (or `<title>`) between 50-60 characters.
   - Every route must include `<meta name="description">` between 150-160 characters.
2. **Open Graph & Twitter Cards**:
   - Include `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image` (1200x630px), and `twitter:card="summary_large_image"`.
3. **Structured Data (JSON-LD)**:
   - Provide Schema.org JSON-LD via `<script type="application/ld+json">`.
   - Prefer `SoftwareApplication`, `Organization`, `FAQPage`, or `BreadcrumbList`.
4. **Heading Hierarchy**:
   - Exactly one `<h1>` per page.
   - Do not skip heading levels (e.g. `<h2>` -> `<h4>`).
5. **Images**:
   - All `<img>` tags must have descriptive `alt` text and explicit `width`/`height` to avoid CLS.
6. **Blazor Component**:
   - In Blazor pages, prefer using `<SeoHeader Title="..." Description="..." CanonicalUrl="..." OgImage="..." />`.

